reference=[('SubagentStop reference', 'The registered tracker extracts agent_id and agent_transcript_path from a real SubagentStop input. This app exposes only Read and launches no subagents. Its offline tracker test uses an explicitly labelled unit fixture; that fixture is not presented as a live SDK event.'), ('Local Slack-format delivery', 'The Notification demo sends a real HTTP POST containing text to a loopback receiver. This verifies payload construction and error handling without external messaging. A real Slack workspace needs its own incoming webhook URL and secret handling; external Slack delivery is not implemented in this sample.'), ('Notification availability', 'Current SDK documentation says permission_prompt occurs after a canUseTool request has waited about six seconds. This app waits roughly nine seconds in the scripted demonstration and verifies the actual Notification callback. Other interactive-only notifications are not assumed to occur.'), ('Async task ownership', 'asyncTimeout is milliseconds; matcher timeout is seconds. Returning async output does not make side effects durable or guarantee delivery. The host tracks each background promise and drains it before final evidence. Background failures are caught and remain visible.'), ('Event-specific timeout outcomes', 'Verified live: PreToolUse timeout blocks the Read, while PostToolUse timeout preserves its result. Late callback output is recorded as an observation, but the SDK discards output after its timeout. Other event outcomes are reference topics: UserPromptSubmit can block the prompt; Stop/SubagentStop count a timeout as no decision; PreModelSwitch can block the switch. Defaults and details depend on runtime version.'), ('Matcher and event troubleshooting', 'Event names are case-sensitive. Tool-event matchers select names such as Read, not lesson.txt. Other events can use different matcher fields, and Stop ignores matchers. Check maxTurns, earlier denial and actual registration before assuming a hook is broken.'), ('Input shape and recursion', 'updatedInput belongs inside hookSpecificOutput with hookEventName. Pairing it with defer discards the update. This app does not modify tool input. A UserPromptSubmit hook that launches work needs a re-entry guard to avoid recursive loops; this app starts no nested agent work.'), ('Scope, cost and cleanup', 'Only a disposable lesson.txt Read is available. The $0.45 SDK budget threshold is not a prepaid cap. Timers, local HTTP connections and pending reviews are settled during cleanup. API keys, dependencies and all teaching media remain excluded from Git.')]
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Every architecture step has source-linked coloured code.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 34 · Hooks in practice\n\nFive linked student pages, large text, actual SDK experiments and coloured code in all thirteen UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson34-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson34-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson34-hooks-practice`. Open http://127.0.0.1:3134 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+, API credit and model access are required. Windows may require Git Bash.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file. Enter your own model key, then restart. Existing shell values take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nNo GitHub token or Managed Agents IDs are required. Secrets, dependencies and teaching media stay outside Git.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, selected lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\n## References\n\n- [Official SDK hooks documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/hooks)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`. Run `npm test` for offline boundaries, review lifecycle, workspace and startup checks.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 34 pages and thirteen source-linked UML steps.')

